Description: network and system administration labs on container machines
 SysResEval (sre) runs teaching labs made of container machines wired
 together: a lab file describes the machines, the networks, the initial
 configuration and the automatic evaluation of what the students did.
 The students work in the sysreseval graphical interface (terminals on the
 machines, course text, questions, evaluations); the instructors write the
 labs, run exams and collect the evaluation archives with the sre command.
 .
 The machines are Docker containers wired by the Kathara framework (the
 default: this package then brings Docker), or rootless Podman containers
 of the sre user (the package sysreseval-podman, which needs no Docker).
 .
 The labs of the project are in /usr/share/sysreseval/lab, the site's own
 labs go in /var/lib/sre/lab; the site parameters are in /etc/sysreseval.

