Description: rootless Podman engine of SysResEval
 What SysResEval needs to run the machines of its labs as rootless Podman
 containers of the sre user, without Docker and without a daemon running as
 root: the switch of the networks (a vde_switch that carries large frames),
 and sysreseval-podman-setup, which prepares the host (the subordinate ids
 and the user manager of the sre user, the image store, the address of the
 host on a host without Docker).  The setup is run when the package is
 installed.
 .
 The engine is then chosen with container_engine = "podman" in
 /etc/sysreseval/params.py (or host by host: container_engine_by_host).

Package: sysreseval-web
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${python3:Depends},
